# Rust
/src-tauri/target/
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock files are committed deliberately. For an application (not a
# library) the lockfile pins the exact dependency graph that gets built
# and shipped, so CI and local builds resolve identically. This also makes
# cargo-deny's advisory results reproducible instead of drifting with
# whatever is newest at resolve time.

# TypeScript
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tauri (no extra rules — src-tauri Cargo.lock is already ignored above)

